WEBVTT

00:00:01.180 --> 00:00:03.230
The Serenity Stellar Monarchy is

00:00:03.230 --> 00:00:05.150
a federation of seven old planets that

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:07.400
have not undergone planetary modification.

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:09.980
The leader of this federation
is the blue planet Serenity.

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:12.650
With an ancient history and
beautiful natural environments,

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:14.990
it truly is a fairy tale kingdom.

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:17.370
But even there, some people

00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:20.040
desire independence from the Galactic Empire.

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:22.750
Amidst these surprisingly complicated circumstances,

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:24.790
the seventh princess, Princess Gruier,

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:28.840
sneaks aboard the Bentenmaru alone, and now...

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:30.760
A ghost ship...

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:34.720
I'd like you to find the wandering golden ghost ship.

00:00:34.990 --> 00:00:36.970
A pirate adventure begins!

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:34.300
I'm getting major energy readings
and combat radar signals from all five ships.

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:35.960
Everyone's ready for a firefight.

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:36.710
They're serious.

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:38.760
Send our transponder data!

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:43.140
Transmitting transponder information.

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:44.260
Now what?

00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:47.020
Full power to sensors and radar.

00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:49.310
Log as much information as you can.

00:02:49.310 --> 00:02:50.940
I don't know what's happening,

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:53.560
but make sure everyone knows that the Bentenmaru is here.

00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:55.780
Roger.

00:02:55.780 --> 00:02:57.570
Initiating combat logging.

00:02:57.570 --> 00:02:59.400
Want to transmit to an off-site backup just in case?

00:02:59.890 --> 00:03:01.240
That's the right call.

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:04.120
Serenity Defense Forces are putting
a lot of power into jamming us.

00:03:04.490 --> 00:03:05.490
Thought so.

00:03:05.490 --> 00:03:07.450
What about the initial Corback?

00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:08.870
I'll put it on your screen.

00:03:10.330 --> 00:03:16.300
It's approaching Tau Ceti at high speed,
heading directly for Sea of the Morningstar.

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:18.920
One Corback is running, and five are chasing.

00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:21.840
One battleship, four escorts.

00:03:22.390 --> 00:03:25.510
Now that they know there's a witness,
they'll prevent us from sending data,

00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:26.510
and then shut us up.

00:03:26.970 --> 00:03:28.140
Which side do we pick?

00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:33.100
Space pirates are the good guys.

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:34.360
Gruier!

00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:36.480
Huh? Uh, yes?

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:40.570
Didn't you mention that you'd
like to wear my uniform?

00:03:41.070 --> 00:03:43.530
Pirates are like soldiers...

00:03:44.030 --> 00:03:46.330
We have to wear uniforms and undertake missions.

00:03:46.910 --> 00:03:51.290
You're going to act as captain for me.

00:03:51.710 --> 00:03:53.620
Hey, it's a pirate queen!

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:55.540
W-What does that mean—

00:03:55.540 --> 00:03:56.880
Here.

00:03:56.880 --> 00:03:58.630
Can we contact the Serenity ships?

00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:02.220
Even if not, you can make it possible, right?

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:03.630
Of course.

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:11.640
A pinpoint directional beam
and we'll be whispering right in their ear.

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:14.270
Okay, ready!

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:16.650
Go on, Princess.

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:19.650
Address your soldiers.

00:04:21.650 --> 00:04:23.110
Right!

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:26.910
Pinpoint transmission beam is ready.

00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:28.120
Locked-on to all six ships.

00:04:28.590 --> 00:04:29.080
Firing.

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:39.050
What are you doing here?!

00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:41.760
I order you in the name of Gruier Serenity,

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:44.720
legitimate heir to the throne of Serenity.

00:04:45.510 --> 00:04:46.680
The glorious...

00:04:47.180 --> 00:04:50.350
The glorious Serenity Defense Forces

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:53.180
are to cease fire immediately!

00:04:53.180 --> 00:04:55.650
Failure to comply will be regarded as treason.

00:04:56.020 --> 00:04:56.980
That is all!

00:04:57.360 --> 00:04:58.820
And that is all.

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:07.490
Good job.

00:05:07.490 --> 00:05:08.700
That's enough.

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:11.490
That was kind of exciting...

00:05:11.490 --> 00:05:12.950
Glad to hear it.

00:05:12.950 --> 00:05:13.580
What's the situation?

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:17.040
The jamming's stopped.

00:05:17.630 --> 00:05:20.130
The energy readings are decreasing too.

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:22.670
All combat functions have been shut down.

00:05:22.670 --> 00:05:24.970
Guess you scared 'em pretty bad.

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:28.890
We're fortunate they're a well-trained army.

00:05:28.890 --> 00:05:31.060
Two of them are hailing us.

00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:32.180
Two of them?

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:35.480
One is the battleship.

00:05:35.480 --> 00:05:37.690
The other is from that first Corback.

00:05:38.690 --> 00:05:42.070
The transmission from the battleship is from their captain.

00:05:42.070 --> 00:05:44.190
The Corback's isn't, though.

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:47.320
"Grand Chamberlain of the Privy Council"?

00:05:47.320 --> 00:05:48.450
It's Yotof.

00:05:49.070 --> 00:05:52.290
Grand Chamberlain of the Privy Council, Yotof Sif Shideux...

00:05:52.290 --> 00:05:56.500
"Your dress is finished, so we've come to deliver it.

00:05:56.500 --> 00:05:58.420
Please try it on."

00:05:58.420 --> 00:05:59.080
What do we do?

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:02.670
Would you put me in touch with Yotof's ship?

00:06:02.670 --> 00:06:05.630
I swear by my royal line that
I will handle any explanations

00:06:05.630 --> 00:06:09.090
and demands that the Serenity ships require.

00:06:09.090 --> 00:06:11.530
Please open a channel.

00:06:11.530 --> 00:06:14.180
That's not a good idea.

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:17.810
Even if they were only firing
at other Serenity ships,

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:21.440
they were firing weapons inside another
star system's absolute defense line.

00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:27.400
If we withhold all information and let them interpret the situation themselves...

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:28.740
It'll give us the advantage!

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:30.160
That's right.

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:32.620
They don't want to make it obvious
what's going on here, either.

00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:36.250
A high-level political decision, huh?

00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:38.960
So I'm sorry, Gruier...

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:42.210
Would you allow my crew to handle this?

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:44.630
Please.

00:06:44.630 --> 00:06:48.970
I'm not terribly accomplished
at foreign relations myself.

00:06:51.340 --> 00:06:53.680
Send a message to the battleship in the princess's name

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:57.180
ordering them to return to stand down,

00:06:57.180 --> 00:06:59.560
return to formation, and stand by.

00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:00.480
Roger!

00:07:02.810 --> 00:07:05.360
As for the Grand Chamberlain
aboard the first Corback,

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:09.030
tell him that the princess is on
her way to pick up the dress.

00:07:09.030 --> 00:07:09.900
Right.

00:07:10.360 --> 00:07:12.660
Kane, you've set the course, right?

00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:15.740
Yup, we're on our way.

00:07:15.740 --> 00:07:16.370
Come to think of it, I'm sorry.

00:07:16.370 --> 00:07:17.870
They've extinguished the fires on the Corback.

00:07:18.330 --> 00:07:20.250
We should have no problem docking.
I'm not very captain-like.

00:07:20.870 --> 00:07:23.880
I realize I'm speaking to you very casually...

00:07:24.670 --> 00:07:26.630
Do you know what I mean by casually?

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:28.970
I do.

00:07:29.920 --> 00:07:33.180
The previous Captain Kato taught me.

00:07:35.510 --> 00:07:37.010
It is my honor

00:07:37.430 --> 00:07:41.850
to have known two generations of pirate captains.

00:07:42.940 --> 00:07:44.610
Please continue to address me that way.

00:07:45.690 --> 00:07:46.570
Roger!

00:08:08.960 --> 00:08:10.260
Yotof...

00:08:19.060 --> 00:08:20.770
Can you tell who it is?

00:08:20.770 --> 00:08:22.770
Grand Chamberlain Yotof.

00:08:22.770 --> 00:08:24.270
I'm certain.

00:08:24.270 --> 00:08:27.570
Behind him is Squad Commander Catherine, of the bodyguards.

00:08:28.110 --> 00:08:30.820
Impossible... Could they have stolen that ship?

00:08:30.820 --> 00:08:32.240
Are they that strong?

00:08:32.240 --> 00:08:33.110
Yes.

00:08:33.110 --> 00:08:34.200
Very strong.

00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:38.200
No weapons or energy signatures detected from them.

00:08:38.620 --> 00:08:40.200
Unarmed?

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:44.040
But their bearings indicate that they are highly trained.

00:08:45.710 --> 00:08:49.340
I'll meet them with real weapons,
not our weapons for show.

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:54.180
I'd like to keep this as peaceful as possible...

00:08:56.930 --> 00:08:58.010
They're here.

00:08:58.600 --> 00:09:00.220
Open the door.

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:11.850
I am Grand Chamberlain of the Privy Council,

00:09:11.850 --> 00:09:13.650
Yotof Sif Shideux.

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:17.700
I am Kato Marika, captain of the Bentenmaru.

00:09:17.700 --> 00:09:20.410
I have brought Princess Gruier Serenity.

00:09:24.040 --> 00:09:25.080
I'm so glad you're safe.

00:09:26.210 --> 00:09:27.880
If you're here, then...

00:09:27.880 --> 00:09:31.090
Nothing has happened at the palace.

00:09:33.590 --> 00:09:37.090
It's been quite peaceful since you left for your study abroad.

00:09:37.090 --> 00:09:41.350
So the two most useless of the people
there have undertaken this mission.

00:09:41.890 --> 00:09:43.100
Do not worry.

00:09:43.100 --> 00:09:44.810
The palace is safe.

00:09:46.350 --> 00:09:47.810
I see.

00:09:47.810 --> 00:09:48.650
I understand.

00:09:49.360 --> 00:09:50.610
Thank you.

00:09:50.610 --> 00:09:51.860
Then show me.

00:09:51.860 --> 00:09:52.780
Yes, Princess.

00:09:57.950 --> 00:09:59.280
Oh, right...

00:09:59.280 --> 00:10:00.830
Thank you.

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:03.830
Please take care of the princess.

00:10:20.340 --> 00:10:21.510
What's wrong?

00:10:21.510 --> 00:10:24.270
I've never seen one in person.

00:10:24.600 --> 00:10:27.730
That's a container used only by the royal family.

00:10:27.730 --> 00:10:31.520
You could probably buy a luxury liner with one of those.

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:37.530
Marika, take this.

00:10:38.400 --> 00:10:42.780
This should contain all the information
we have on the golden ghost ship.

00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:50.960
The golden ghost ship...

00:11:05.970 --> 00:11:08.230
Okay, I might make it today!

00:11:08.230 --> 00:11:09.980
I could be... I could be...

00:11:10.640 --> 00:11:11.980
the first person here!

00:11:14.770 --> 00:11:16.030
Chiaki?

00:11:18.900 --> 00:11:20.240
Chiaki!

00:11:20.610 --> 00:11:23.070
I told you not to call me that...

00:11:23.070 --> 00:11:24.200
I missed you, Chiaki!

00:11:24.200 --> 00:11:25.330
Stop!

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:25.780
Stop it!

00:11:27.200 --> 00:11:31.080
We were both training,
and then you just left.

00:11:31.080 --> 00:11:33.460
And you met Mami without saying anything.

00:11:33.460 --> 00:11:34.890
It's not fair!

00:11:36.590 --> 00:11:41.220
You aren't the only one who's
both a space pirate and a student.

00:11:41.220 --> 00:11:45.300
I heard you got caught up in
some Serenity power struggles.

00:11:45.300 --> 00:11:46.810
I'm surprised you know about that.

00:11:46.810 --> 00:11:47.850
I know all about it.

00:11:47.850 --> 00:11:48.390
Interstellar Diplomatic Law

00:11:48.390 --> 00:11:51.310
That's why I'm staying here and researching.

00:11:51.810 --> 00:11:55.900
I just came to this planet because my dad
asked me to buy him some tea and alcohol.

00:11:56.360 --> 00:11:58.400
And some parfaits? At the Lamp House?

00:12:00.900 --> 00:12:02.280
I see.

00:12:02.280 --> 00:12:04.990
I guess it's become kind of famous.

00:12:04.990 --> 00:12:10.750
But I think it might be a little different than what you think...

00:12:11.210 --> 00:12:12.670
I know that.

00:12:12.670 --> 00:12:14.960
Only those directly involved know the truth.

00:12:15.380 --> 00:12:18.170
We were hired to search for the ghost ship too.

00:12:20.090 --> 00:12:22.970
The job came to us via an underground route,

00:12:22.970 --> 00:12:25.220
so the real client is unknown.

00:12:25.220 --> 00:12:26.600
A ghost ship?

00:12:27.010 --> 00:12:29.390
Serenity's golden ghost ship.

00:12:29.390 --> 00:12:32.940
Find it, and eliminate anyone in our way.

00:12:33.640 --> 00:12:36.020
I didn't read the official contract,

00:12:36.020 --> 00:12:40.440
but they want us to eliminate anyone
else looking for it in outer space,

00:12:40.440 --> 00:12:41.490
I think.

00:12:43.490 --> 00:12:47.240
So that's what we're up against, huh?

00:12:47.240 --> 00:12:49.330
Thanks for telling me.

00:12:49.700 --> 00:12:52.450
You understand, we don't know
where the job originated, right?

00:12:52.450 --> 00:12:54.790
I'm just searching for more information.

00:12:54.790 --> 00:12:56.920
Then did you go to the middle school?

00:12:56.920 --> 00:12:58.630
Did you see the princess?

00:12:58.630 --> 00:12:59.370
Not interested.

00:12:59.370 --> 00:13:01.010
Oh, don't be silly.

00:13:01.840 --> 00:13:03.010
Come on...

00:13:03.340 --> 00:13:05.220
I'm not into that stuff!

00:13:07.180 --> 00:13:08.850
Come in!

00:13:10.180 --> 00:13:11.310
Excuse me.

00:13:11.720 --> 00:13:13.060
Gruier?

00:13:15.730 --> 00:13:18.520
A pleasure to meet you.
I am Gruier Serenity.

00:13:22.530 --> 00:13:24.360
An honor, Princess.

00:13:24.700 --> 00:13:26.990
Hey, you're really into it, Chiaki!

00:13:26.990 --> 00:13:28.570
Don't call me that!

00:13:30.530 --> 00:13:33.200
Oh, it's Kurihara Chiaki!

00:13:33.200 --> 00:13:33.970
Chiaki!

00:13:33.970 --> 00:13:35.160
It's Chiaki!

00:13:35.160 --> 00:13:36.040
Chiaki!

00:13:36.040 --> 00:13:37.220
Hey, Chiaki!

00:13:37.220 --> 00:13:37.750
Chiaki!

00:13:37.750 --> 00:13:39.630
Stop that...

00:13:42.500 --> 00:13:44.090
I am Gruier Serenity.

00:13:44.090 --> 00:13:45.670
This again...

00:13:46.180 --> 00:13:48.470
I'm the club president, Jenny Dolittle.

00:13:48.470 --> 00:13:50.390
We've met before.

00:13:50.390 --> 00:13:53.350
I'm amazed you remember.

00:13:53.350 --> 00:13:57.600
We were introduced at the opening
of the new Arnold Junction route.

00:13:57.980 --> 00:13:59.230
That's correct.

00:13:59.230 --> 00:14:01.690
Hugh and Dolittle Interstellar Transportation

00:14:01.690 --> 00:14:03.190
has been good to my nation.

00:14:03.480 --> 00:14:05.530
Oh, it's a different world.

00:14:05.820 --> 00:14:10.620
So what brings a princess to
the high school yacht club?

00:14:12.240 --> 00:14:14.870
Well, um, actually...

00:14:15.750 --> 00:14:18.290
According to certain information I've acquired,

00:14:18.290 --> 00:14:21.170
one of the yacht club members

00:14:21.170 --> 00:14:25.760
is a master of the illegal skill "faking attendance."

00:14:26.880 --> 00:14:27.720
Oh, my.

00:14:28.680 --> 00:14:30.180
Faking attendance?

00:14:30.180 --> 00:14:30.930
Who told you?

00:14:31.350 --> 00:14:34.930
It was a place called the Lamp House,
which serves lovely tea and parfaits...

00:14:35.930 --> 00:14:36.770
It was her.

00:14:37.430 --> 00:14:41.770
You see, the yacht club has all kinds

00:14:41.770 --> 00:14:44.070
of talented people there!

00:14:44.070 --> 00:14:46.690
I'm sure one of them can help you!

00:14:49.860 --> 00:14:53.700
Mami, what do you think we are?

00:14:53.700 --> 00:14:55.700
I think she has the right idea.

00:14:55.700 --> 00:15:00.790
Not many high school girls can win at
electronic warfare on their first practice cruise.

00:15:00.790 --> 00:15:03.380
Oh, so you're defending Mami.

00:15:03.380 --> 00:15:05.340
I'm not defending her.

00:15:05.340 --> 00:15:07.170
I'm just saying that if you need

00:15:07.170 --> 00:15:09.930
something illegal at this high school,
this club is the place to go.

00:15:10.300 --> 00:15:14.140
But it's kind of depressing that
she was sent here to fake attendance...

00:15:14.140 --> 00:15:16.140
Ah, is there a problem?

00:15:16.560 --> 00:15:20.770
Princess, may I ask why you
wish to sabotage your classes?

00:15:21.520 --> 00:15:26.570
I can't share the details,
but in the future, I may need

00:15:26.570 --> 00:15:30.740
to leave school for a short,
or even extended, period.

00:15:31.570 --> 00:15:33.660
During that time,

00:15:33.660 --> 00:15:36.660
I'd like people to think I'm still
attending Hakuoh Academy.

00:15:38.080 --> 00:15:40.790
Doesn't this concern you too?

00:15:40.790 --> 00:15:44.130
The princess will be accompanying you, right?

00:15:44.130 --> 00:15:45.710
I see.

00:15:45.710 --> 00:15:48.880
So you'll be with Marika for her work, right?

00:15:48.880 --> 00:15:49.470
Yes.

00:15:49.470 --> 00:15:52.300
Then that's easy!

00:15:52.300 --> 00:15:54.470
Luckily, there's going to be a practice cruise

00:15:54.470 --> 00:15:59.220
over the post-exam break
to send us third-year students off.

00:15:59.850 --> 00:16:01.060
When did we plan that?

00:16:01.060 --> 00:16:02.570
Just now.

00:16:04.480 --> 00:16:05.940
And so, from now on,

00:16:05.940 --> 00:16:08.230
Miss Gruier is a yacht club member!

00:16:09.570 --> 00:16:10.150
Oh, my!

00:16:12.820 --> 00:16:14.490
Will that work?

00:16:14.820 --> 00:16:17.330
Yes, thank you.

00:16:17.330 --> 00:16:18.080
And...

00:16:18.450 --> 00:16:19.540
What is it?

00:16:20.160 --> 00:16:23.370
Thank you for calling me "Gruier."

00:16:23.750 --> 00:16:28.300
We have upperclassmen and underclassmen,
but basically, the yacht club is equal.

00:16:28.840 --> 00:16:30.550
Nice to meet you, Gruier!

00:16:30.550 --> 00:16:32.130
Nice to meet you, Gruier.

00:16:32.130 --> 00:16:33.050
Hi!

00:16:33.050 --> 00:16:33.760
Yo!

00:16:33.760 --> 00:16:34.180
Welcome!

00:16:34.180 --> 00:16:35.840
Thank you, everyone!

00:16:35.840 --> 00:16:36.890
I look forward to working with you.

00:16:36.890 --> 00:16:38.390
All together...

00:16:39.100 --> 00:16:41.730
Let's start by taking Gruier to the Simulation Dome!

00:16:43.690 --> 00:16:48.440
We are Hakuoh, a white...

00:16:48.980 --> 00:16:51.440
But are we really doing this practice cruise?

00:16:51.990 --> 00:16:53.950
It's also convenient for you, isn't it?

00:16:53.950 --> 00:16:54.780
During that time, I mean.

00:16:55.160 --> 00:16:57.240
Yes, it is, but...

00:16:57.240 --> 00:16:59.620
That way, you can focus on your studies.

00:17:00.900 --> 00:17:03.710
I saw your second semester grades.

00:17:03.710 --> 00:17:04.330
They're terrible.

00:17:04.920 --> 00:17:06.920
Even if they are getting better.

00:17:06.920 --> 00:17:08.790
Have you been hacking again?

00:17:09.170 --> 00:17:11.260
Let's all do our best, Marika.

00:17:11.260 --> 00:17:14.340
At our studies, at our club, and at being a pirate.

00:17:14.970 --> 00:17:17.090
Yes, I'll do my best.

00:17:17.090 --> 00:17:19.010
Do, really.

00:17:22.680 --> 00:17:24.430
I'm back.

00:17:24.430 --> 00:17:26.650
Sending Mail

00:17:28.020 --> 00:17:29.360
Welcome back.

00:17:29.360 --> 00:17:30.730
Huh?

00:17:32.110 --> 00:17:33.690
Where's dinner?

00:17:33.690 --> 00:17:35.240
We're eating out tonight.

00:17:35.240 --> 00:17:36.860
What should I wear?

00:17:37.360 --> 00:17:38.740
That outfit's fine.

00:17:38.740 --> 00:17:39.830
Now let's go.

00:17:45.870 --> 00:17:48.460
You haven't been under the airport
in a long time, have you?

00:17:49.460 --> 00:17:50.710
It's just like it was.

00:17:53.590 --> 00:17:54.090
This is the place.

00:17:55.300 --> 00:17:56.800
I think I remember this...

00:18:08.770 --> 00:18:10.310
Hi, there.

00:18:12.230 --> 00:18:13.320
Welcome.

00:18:14.820 --> 00:18:17.150
It's been a while, boss.

00:18:17.150 --> 00:18:19.160
Everyone's already here.

00:18:19.530 --> 00:18:20.910
Do you remember her?

00:18:20.910 --> 00:18:22.740
This is my daughter, Marika.

00:18:25.910 --> 00:18:27.210
Hi.

00:18:30.540 --> 00:18:32.290
Don't knock anything over.

00:18:35.510 --> 00:18:36.170
Who's that?

00:18:36.470 --> 00:18:38.430
The manager of the cafeteria district.

00:18:38.430 --> 00:18:40.890
In other words, the airport's most powerful person.

00:18:41.350 --> 00:18:43.600
I knew it. Food is strong.

00:18:45.140 --> 00:18:46.060
They're here.

00:18:46.480 --> 00:18:48.270
Gruier, are you okay?

00:18:49.440 --> 00:18:51.150
Yes, I am.

00:18:56.280 --> 00:19:00.030
San-Daime is still on the Bentenmaru, just in case.

00:19:00.030 --> 00:19:01.410
So, this is everyone.

00:19:01.410 --> 00:19:02.620
Then let's begin.

00:19:02.910 --> 00:19:04.280
Did you analyze the data?

00:19:04.580 --> 00:19:05.950
Finally.

00:19:05.950 --> 00:19:09.500
The royal family's data is highly protected,

00:19:09.500 --> 00:19:10.500
and there's a lot of it.

00:19:11.290 --> 00:19:14.800
It took me a long time to organize it all.

00:19:17.550 --> 00:19:19.630
The golden ghost ship of Serenity!

00:19:20.430 --> 00:19:24.100
In reality, it is the first colony ship to carry passengers.

00:19:24.430 --> 00:19:27.470
It was made long ago, before modern
technologies like inertial control

00:19:27.810 --> 00:19:30.890
and faster than light speed travel even existed.

00:19:31.480 --> 00:19:35.070
Interstellar flight would take years.

00:19:35.070 --> 00:19:37.860
So cold sleep was a necessity.

00:19:38.150 --> 00:19:40.400
They probably made all kinds of modifications

00:19:40.400 --> 00:19:43.070
to allow for a journey of many light years,

00:19:43.070 --> 00:19:45.160
which would take entire generations.

00:19:45.580 --> 00:19:49.540
This is how it looked, the last
time a search team found it.

00:19:52.080 --> 00:19:54.210
So that's the ghost ship.

00:19:54.580 --> 00:19:55.840
It's big, huh?

00:19:55.840 --> 00:19:57.550
Who knows how many towns could fit in that.

00:19:58.760 --> 00:20:03.760
This is a plot of all sightings of the
golden ghost ship over the past two hundred years.

00:20:04.050 --> 00:20:08.220
And from these, we can predict its probable route.

00:20:11.310 --> 00:20:12.100
Hey, hey.

00:20:12.100 --> 00:20:13.190
Oh, how awful.

00:20:13.690 --> 00:20:18.150
Dark nebulae, overlapping black holes,
dwarf star clusters, and proto-planets.

00:20:18.150 --> 00:20:19.780
Navigating around any of those alone would be difficult.

00:20:20.150 --> 00:20:20.990
That's right.

00:20:20.990 --> 00:20:23.910
That's why not everyone can see it.

00:20:24.450 --> 00:20:28.330
No one knows why this route was chosen.

00:20:31.930 --> 00:20:33.370
W-What are you doing?

00:20:33.870 --> 00:20:37.420
It doesn't matter now why it's a ghost ship.

00:20:37.420 --> 00:20:41.260
Our client is here, and we have
all the information we can get.

00:20:41.260 --> 00:20:43.340
All that remains is to act.

00:20:43.340 --> 00:20:45.470
We don't want to keep the chef waiting.

00:20:52.890 --> 00:20:52.980
Gruier, even if we set out,
we may not find the ghost ship.

00:20:52.980 --> 00:20:57.610
True darkness feels so empty.

00:20:57.610 --> 00:20:58.610
Are you still okay with that?

00:20:59.400 --> 00:21:00.400
I can't even see my own palm.

00:21:00.400 --> 00:21:02.610
I believe in you, Marika.

00:21:02.610 --> 00:21:04.320
And in the golden ghost ship.

00:21:04.320 --> 00:21:06.070
I can't even see my own palm.

00:21:06.660 --> 00:21:08.780
The stars above are the only light.

00:21:08.780 --> 00:21:10.740
Are you finished talking?

00:21:10.740 --> 00:21:12.500
I'd like to serve the food.
The stars above are the only light.

00:21:12.910 --> 00:21:12.950
Please do.

00:21:12.950 --> 00:21:17.790
My senses sharpen again, like a wild animal's.

00:21:17.790 --> 00:21:19.420
Bring on the drinks!

00:21:19.420 --> 00:21:20.090
My senses sharpen again, like a wild animal's.

00:21:20.090 --> 00:21:20.590
So the pirate ship is carrying a princess
to look for a ghost ship, huh?

00:21:20.590 --> 00:21:23.300
My conscience heads inward, inward

00:21:23.300 --> 00:21:24.420
on an arduous, testing journey.

00:21:24.420 --> 00:21:26.760
The job's a lot more romantic
than the ones I used to get.

00:21:26.760 --> 00:21:30.470
The fragile blade I believed in

00:21:30.470 --> 00:21:31.640
lost its shine.

00:21:31.640 --> 00:21:35.770
I hope it doesn't turn into
an action movie or a huge spectacle.

00:21:35.770 --> 00:21:42.730
Into the holy space I throw myself.

00:21:42.730 --> 00:21:49.320
Find the answer no matter how hard, Black Holy.

00:21:49.320 --> 00:21:49.410
Even if the horizons of the distant space are gone,

00:21:49.410 --> 00:21:50.990
Let's go, everyone.

00:21:50.990 --> 00:21:54.410
Set sail for the golden ghost ship of Serenity!

00:21:54.410 --> 00:21:56.080
Even if the horizons of the distant space are gone,

00:21:56.500 --> 00:22:01.210
I feel no fear.

00:22:01.210 --> 00:22:04.970
I feel free.

00:22:08.510 --> 00:22:11.720
A Beautiful Launch

00:22:13.350 --> 00:22:19.810
Close your eyes and race the wind.

00:22:19.810 --> 00:22:27.240
The runway is the path from the land to my soul.

00:22:27.240 --> 00:22:30.240
Outwards, outwards the pulses

00:22:30.240 --> 00:22:33.790
go on rippling waves on the way.

00:22:33.790 --> 00:22:37.080
Everything that can help me

00:22:37.080 --> 00:22:41.040
is supporting me as I progress.

00:22:42.790 --> 00:22:49.680
Even if the borders of the soul of space are hazy,

00:22:49.680 --> 00:22:54.390
I feel no fear.

00:22:54.390 --> 00:22:59.770
I feel free.

00:23:02.980 --> 00:23:05.360
I feel it...

00:23:09.950 --> 00:23:18.410
Into the future beyond the holy chaos,

00:23:18.410 --> 00:23:26.550
I will go on, never worrying about who I am.

00:23:38.350 --> 00:23:40.440
Amidst swirling tides and black clouds,

00:23:40.440 --> 00:23:42.060
friend and enemy collide.

00:23:42.810 --> 00:23:45.190
Is the captain's judgment courageous or brash?

00:23:45.190 --> 00:23:46.480
The blood of royals.

00:23:46.480 --> 00:23:48.650
The blood of pirates.

00:23:48.650 --> 00:23:53.070
What fate awaits the two girls?

00:23:54.570 --> 00:23:56.280
Next time, on <i>Bodacious Space Pirates:</i>

00:23:56.280 --> 00:23:57.620
Battle in the storm.

00:23:57.620 --> 00:23:58.950
Look forward to it.

00:23:58.950 --> 00:24:04.960
Battle in the Storm

00:24:04.960 --> 00:24:10.460
The illegal skill "faking attendance"
